entries.query:
Generate a complete, unabridged, production-ready, single-file HTML application containing CSS and JavaScript for a highly advanced AI chat interface. The application must include a custom WebGL2-based rendering engine that perfectly synchronizes a physical glass-morphism effect with the HTML DOM elements [cite: 728-780]. Do not use simplified, mock, placeholder, dummy, simulated, or fake content.
### 1. HTML Layout and Structure
 * [cite_start]Set the document to support mobile web app capabilities with viewport fit cover and translucent status bars.
 * Include a root container div with the ID #app [cite: 32-33].
 * [cite_start]Create a sidebar element (#sidebar) for conversation history, complete with a search bar (#sb-search-bar), a "new chat" button (#btn-sb-new), and a history list (#hlist) [cite: 46-48, 62, 79, 305].
 * [cite_start]Construct a main content area (#content) containing a scrollable message list (#msg-list) [cite: 110-115, 307].
 * [cite_start]Implement an input wrapper (#ib-wrap) fixed to the bottom, containing an image/file strip (#img-strip), a gallery attachment button (#btn-gal), a multiline textarea (#ta), and a send button (#sbtn) [cite: 159-161, 162-164, 170-192, 307-310].
 * [cite_start]Add modal UI overlays: a toast notification container (#toasts) [cite: 197-199][cite_start], an action sheet (#action-sheet) [cite: 221-222, 306][cite_start], and a custom context menu (#ctx-menu) [cite: 212-214].
 * [cite_start]Place a <canvas> with the ID glass-renderer-canvas fixed in the background behind all elements [cite: 288-290].
### 2. CSS Styling
 * [cite_start]Define a robust set of CSS variables for both dark (default) and light color schemes (--bg, --fg, --liquid, --sep, etc.) [cite: 3-13]. [cite_start]Utilize env(safe-area-inset-*) for mobile screen notches.
 * Style user messages (.u .bubble) with a distinct gradient background, rounded corners, and inner box-shadows [cite: 120-123]. [cite_start]Style AI messages (.ai-bubble) without backgrounds [cite: 123-124].
 * [cite_start]Style standard markdown elements: headers, paragraphs, bold, italic, code blocks, unordered/ordered lists, and tables with borders [cite: 124-136, 248-254].
 * [cite_start]Create CSS animations: tbounce for a three-dot typing indicator [cite: 147-152][cite_start], spin for loading states [cite: 271-273][cite_start], and tin for toast appearance [cite: 206-208].
 * [cite_start]Define a .glass-host override block that strips backgrounds, borders, and backdrop-filters from specific UI elements (e.g., .lg, .bubble, #sidebar) so the WebGL canvas can render their visual properties [cite: 292-295].
### 3. Core Application Logic (Vanilla JS)
 * [cite_start]Implement a custom Markdown parser that handles bold, italic, lists (ordered/unordered), headers, and horizontal rules, generating secure HTML [cite: 341-352]. [cite_start]Integrate highlight.js for code block syntax highlighting [cite: 2, 353-354].
 * [cite_start]Manage local state utilizing localStorage to save chat history metadata (chat:hmeta) and deleted message tracking (chat:deleted) [cite: 375-378]. [cite_start]Implement history sorting and pinning [cite: 374, 657-658].
 * [cite_start]Handle file attachments by compressing images via an off-screen <canvas> before converting them to Data URLs, and parsing text files as strings [cite: 465-472, 477-478]. [cite_start]Support pasting images directly into the textarea [cite: 493-495].
 * [cite_start]Build touch gesture logic: a swipe right/left gesture to open/close the sidebar [cite: 415-429][cite_start], and a pull-down gesture in the sidebar to reveal the search bar [cite: 411-414].
 * [cite_start]Implement dynamic UI behaviors: auto-resize the textarea based on content [cite: 498-500][cite_start], scroll to the bottom automatically when near the end [cite: 322-324][cite_start], and handle context menus on messages for copying, editing, or deleting [cite: 699-712].
### 4. API Integration and Streaming
 * [cite_start]Manage API calls to /api/chat using the Fetch API. [cite_start]Handle Server-Sent Events (SSE) by parsing data: chunks manually [cite: 523-527].
 * [cite_start]Implement automatic exponential backoff for failed network requests [cite: 564-566, 583-587].
 * [cite_start]Process specialized SSE event types such as session, job_id, search_start, sources, and content, dynamically updating the DOM to show search chips and appended markdown [cite: 538-557].
 * [cite_start]Check for and resume active background jobs via /api/job/.../status and /api/agent/resume/... when the page loads or becomes visible [cite: 612-635, 727].
### 5. WebGL2 Rendering Engine
 * [cite_start]Initialize a WebGL2 context requiring the EXT_color_buffer_float extension [cite: 728-729].
 * Construct a MultiPassRenderer class managing three GLSL shader passes:
   1. [cite_start]**Background Pass:** Render an animated gradient noise pattern [cite: 730-731].
   2. [cite_start]**Blur Pass:** Execute a two-pass (horizontal and vertical) Gaussian blur using an array of computed weights based on a customizable blur radius [cite: 732-734, 754-757].
   3. **Main Pass:** Generate the final glass effect using Signed Distance Fields (SDF). [cite_start]Calculate normals from the SDF to create realistic refraction, apply fresnel edges, and render directional glare [cite: 739-746].
 * [cite_start]In the JavaScript animation loop, use getBoundingClientRect() to track elements matching specific selectors (e.g., .lg, .bubble, #sidebar) [cite: 766-770]. [cite_start]Pass up to 128 bounding boxes and border-radii into the shader via uniform4fv and uniform1fv arrays to perfectly sync the visual glass blocks with the HTML DOM [cite: 761, 775-776, 781].



